/* PARKED 2026-09-07 -- first session on this function; it was never opened
 * before (it is one of the three main functions §B8 names as clean of every
 * wall).  State, measured with the compile-only masked shape diff (§D 2b,
 * registers anchored, immediates masked, difflib-aligned, running offset
 * printed): **912 vs 913 insns, 203 masked mismatches over 89 regions, final
 * offset -1**.  Trajectory this session: 300/110/+18 (first decode, would not
 * link) -> 276/105/-4 (A200 barrier) -> 270 (byte-offset rect walk) -> 231/88
 * (barrier moved to P1) -> 225 (cosine load hoisted) -> **203/89/-1**.
 *
 * IT LINKS.  Linked positional credit is only 244 bytes (61/913 words) because
 * the running offset wanders +-6 through the middle -- §C's positional trap.
 * The next session's objective is the OFFSET PROFILE, not the mismatch count.
 *
 * ---- The five levers that are already in and are load-bearing --------------
 * 1. **A200 barrier position, swept.**  The gem machine reaches five different
 *    globals off ONE base ($a2 = &g_dwHudBobSinePhase, offsets -0x3C/-0x37/
 *    -0x30/-0x1C/0), which is §B-i rule 1 territory: without a cse ebb-break
 *    every nonzero offset folded to `lui $at; sb %lo(sym+off)($at)`.  The
 *    empty `do { } while (0);` restores all 18 register-based accesses.  Its
 *    POSITION is worth 43 masked mismatches: measured at the three legal slots
 *    (after `BOB = nPhase;` / after the 0x1A6 store / after the 0x1A5 store)
 *    it scores **231 / 241 / 274**.  The winner is the earliest one, i.e.
 *    immediately after the offset-0 access that materialises the base.
 * 2. The alias MUST be reached as an incomplete ARRAY with element indices.  A
 *    pointer local seeded from it (`unsigned char *hud = ...Block;`) was
 *    measured at 303 against the array form's 300 -- reload's
 *    `update_equiv_regs` folds through the pointer's REG_EQUIV note, exactly as
 *    A200's condition 1 says.
 * 3. **The butterfly ring walk is a BYTE offset, not a short index** (A179 /
 *    A35).  `g_anHudSpriteRects[k]`/`[k+1]`/`[k+2]`/`[k+3]` with `k += 4` makes
 *    loop.c hand each of the four field accesses its OWN pointer giv (four
 *    `addiu rN,rN,8` per iteration).  Writing them as
 *    `*(short *)((char *)g_anHudSpriteRects + k)` with `k += 8` keeps the
 *    original's single scaled index register and puts the field constant back
 *    in `%lo(sym+K)($at)`.  Worth 6 masked and, more importantly, 10 insns of
 *    positional offset inside the loop.
 * 4. **The roll-out arms need a named decrement carrier** (A164 step 1).
 *    `SYM -= 1; Offset(..., tbl[SYM]);` puts the argument copy in the branch
 *    delay slot and the decrement inside the block; `j = SYM - 1; SYM = j;
 *    Offset(..., tbl[(unsigned char)j]);` puts the DECREMENT in the delay slot,
 *    which is what the original has.  22 masked mismatches across the five
 *    machines, and it took the final offset from -5 to -1.
 * 5. The cosine load is hoisted into `nCos` so it precedes the 0x1A6 store,
 *    which is the original's order (6 masked).
 *
 * ---- The dominant residue: OUR BYTE-GLOBAL STORES SINK -------------------
 * ~40 of the 203, and it is the same shape at six sites: the original emits
 * `lui $at; sb rX,%lo(sym)($at)` immediately after the value is computed and
 * BEFORE the `andi/sll/lh` chain that re-reads it (cse having turned the
 * re-read into the `andi`); we emit the whole chain first and the store just
 * above the `jal`.  Sites: the five roll-out arms (orig[222]/[317]/[502]/
 * [704]/[855], each `-3 +1` then `+2` a few insns later) and the
 * `g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x411] += 4` spin at orig[867].
 * Read off §D 2d: sched2 schedules BACKWARD and `schedule_select` picks the
 * largest `potential_hazard` in the first priority group -- a store beats a
 * load beats an ALU op -- so a store that is READY early is placed LAST.
 * Ruled out this session:
 *   - hoisting the decrement above the test with a comma operator
 *     (`} else if (j = SYM - 1, SYM == 0) {`), which was meant to make the
 *     store's operand live-in and drop its priority to 1: **byte-identical**
 *     to the baseline, 203/89 either way.
 *   - `*(volatile unsigned char *)&SYM = j;` at all five sites (A239): does
 *     NOT pin the store (it still lands below the `lh`), and although it makes
 *     the function length-EXACT (913/913, final offset 0) it re-tiles
 *     everything from orig[229] on and the linked positional credit FALLS from
 *     244 to 148 bytes.  Kept out for that reason; try it per-site.
 * The untried probe is the one §D 2d prescribes: a `-dR` (`<in>.i.sched2`)
 * trace of one roll-out block, to see whether the store is losing on priority
 * or on `potential_hazard`.  That is where the next session should start.
 *
 * ---- The other named residues --------------------------------------------
 * R2  ONE EXTRA CALLEE-SAVED REGISTER (2 insns + a whole-function rotation).
 *     We save ra/s3/s2/s1/s0, the original saves ra/s2/s1/s0.  The extra one
 *     holds the level-egg spawn loop's `0x01000000` increment, which loop.c
 *     hoists for us and the original re-materialises inline as
 *     `lui v0,0x100; addu s0,s0,v0` per iteration (the §B10 direction).  The
 *     original pays for that with a stack slot instead: its `vars` is 24 bytes
 *     against our 16, for the same `av[3]`, i.e. one 8-byte reload spill slot
 *     (§C).  So this is a register-PRESSURE difference, not a spelling: the
 *     original has one more live value somewhere than we do.  A245 (separate
 *     counters for the butterfly and spawn loops) is already applied and did
 *     not close it.
 * R3  The head is byte-aligned through orig[25]; what is left is the absolute
 *     re-read `lui v1,%hi(bob); lw v1,%lo(bob)` (orig[26..27]) sitting ABOVE
 *     the 0x1A6 store in the original and below it in ours -- a 4-insn
 *     displacement the barrier at P1 imposes, since the two are then in
 *     different blocks (A200's "source order is the emitted order" corollary).
 * R4  The butterfly loop still emits the two `sh t0` constant stores before the
 *     first computed store (orig[519..546], -12/+10).  Same store-ordering
 *     family as the dominant residue; the four store statements' source order
 *     has NOT been swept (24 orders, ~20 s each).
 *
 * ---- Decode notes (all verified against the asm, not m2c) -----------------
 *  - Switches 1-3 (gems / dragons / lives) are if/else-if LADDERS: the asm
 *    tests 0,1,2,3,4 linearly.  Switches 4-5 (world eggs / level eggs) are real
 *    `switch` statements -- gcc emits `balance_case_nodes`' binary tree
 *    (`beq 1; slti 2; beqz 0; ...`) and, with four cases, no jump table, so
 *    there is no §B8 rodata problem in this function.
 *  - `g_abHudCounterDisplayState` is byte[5] and every roll-phase/timer global
 *    is <= 8 bytes, so they are all sdata cost 1 and fold to absolute unless
 *    an incomplete-array alias is used (A22).  Four new aliases were added to
 *    symbol_addrs.txt for this function; three more already existed.
 *  - The function is void: the epilogue leaves whatever was last in $v0.
 */
#include "globals.h"

/* 0x80054988, 3652 bytes — the per-frame HUD tick.  Bobs the two sine-driven
   icon anchors, then runs five independent roll-animation state machines (one
   per counter: level gems, dragons, lives+butterflies, world eggs, level eggs)
   out of g_abHudCounterDisplayState[0..4].  Each machine is the same four
   states: 0 idle (watch the live value), 1 roll-in (14 steps off
   g_anHudRollInStepTable), 2 hold/ratchet (advance the cached count toward the
   live one, driving the digit glyphs through SetHudCounterDigits +
   CommitHudCounterAnimState), 3 roll-out (14 steps off
   g_anHudRollOutStepTable).  Between the lives and world-egg machines it lays
   the sparx-food butterflies out around their ring, and it closes by converting
   every 20 butterflies into an extra life (capped at 99). */

extern void SetHudCounterDigits(int nFirstSlot, int nSlots, int nValue,
                                int bCommit);
extern void CommitHudCounterAnimState(int nFirstSlot, int nSlots, int nPhase);
extern void OffsetHudIconRollAxis(int nFirstSlot, int nSlots, int nOffset);
extern void OffsetHudDigitRollAxis(int nFirstSlot, int nSlots, int nOffset);

extern short g_anCosineLut[]; /* g_anSineLut + 0x80 */

/* Held-base views (A20/A22/A25).  The original materializes ONE base per group
   and reaches the neighbours off it; every other site of the same address stays
   on the plain absolute symbol, which is the per-site A240 split. */
extern unsigned char g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock[];   /* 0x80077fe4 */
extern unsigned char g_anHudLevelGemCachedBlock[];  /* 0x80077fc8 */
extern unsigned char g_abHudGemRollPhaseBlock[];    /* 0x80077fad */
extern unsigned char g_abHudWorldEggIconBlock[];    /* 0x80077fab, state[3] */
extern unsigned char g_abHudLevelEggCounterBlock[]; /* 0x80077fac, state[4] */
extern int g_anHudButterflyCachedBlock[];           /* 0x80077fe0 */
extern int g_anHudWorldEggTimerBlock[];             /* 0x80077fc0 */
extern int g_anHudLevelEggTimerBlock[];             /* 0x80077fc4 */

/* the bob-phase base reaches the whole gem machine's state at -0x3C..-0x1C */
#define HUD g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock
#define BOB (*(unsigned int *)&HUD[0])
#define GEM_STATE (HUD[-0x3C])
#define GEM_PHASE (HUD[-0x37])
#define GEM_TIMER (*(int *)&HUD[-0x30])
#define GEM_CACHED (*(int *)&HUD[-0x1C])

/* the gem cached-count base reaches the roll phase at -0x1B */
#define GEMCACHE (*(int *)&g_anHudLevelGemCachedBlock[0])
#define GEMCACHE_PHASE (g_anHudLevelGemCachedBlock[-0x1B])

/* the sprite-rect walk is a BYTE offset off the array, which keeps one
   scaled index register and the field constant in %lo(sym+K) (A179/A35) */
#define RECT(off) (*(short *)((char *)g_anHudSpriteRects + (off)))

#define EGG_STATE (g_abHudWorldEggIconBlock[0])
#define LEGG_STATE (g_abHudLevelEggCounterBlock[0])

void UpdateHudCounters(void) {
  int nPhase;
  int nDelta;
  int i;
  int n;
  int j;
  int k;
  int nTint;
  int nCos;
  int av[3];

  g_nHudFrameCycleMod9 = (g_nHudFrameCycleMod9 + 1) % 9;
  nPhase = (BOB - g_nFrameStep) & 0xFF;
  BOB = nPhase;
  do {
  } while (0); /* A200 cse ebb-break: keeps the gem block's
                  -0x3C..-0x1C accesses on the held base (swept: this
                  position beats the two later ones by 43 and 10) */
  nCos = g_anCosineLut[g_dwHudBobSinePhase];
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x1A6] = nPhase;
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x1A5] = nCos >> 9;

  /* --- counter 0: level gems ------------------------------------------ */
  if (GEM_STATE == 0) {
    if (GEM_CACHED != g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex]) {
      GEM_STATE = 1;
      GEM_PHASE = 0;
    }
  } else if (GEM_STATE == 1) {
    j = g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase & 0xFF;
    if (j == 0xD) {
      GEM_STATE = 2;
      g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase = 0;
      GEM_TIMER = 0;
      if (GEM_CACHED == g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex]) {
        GEM_TIMER = -0x28;
      }
    } else {
      g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase = j + 1;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(0, 5, g_anHudRollInStepTable[j]);
    }
  } else if (GEM_STATE == 2) {
    if (GEM_CACHED == g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex] &&
        GEM_PHASE == 0) {
      GEM_TIMER = GEM_TIMER + 1;
      if (GEM_TIMER == 0x14) {
        GEM_STATE = 3;
        GEM_PHASE = 0xD;
      }
    } else {
      g_nHudLevelGemHoldTimer = 0;
      if (g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex] -
                  g_nHudLevelGemCachedCount >=
              3 &&
          (g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase & 0x1F) == 0) {
        g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase -= 0x20;
      } else {
        g_abHudGemRollPhaseBlock[0] -= 0x10;
      }
      SetHudCounterDigits(0, 4, GEMCACHE + 1, 0);
      CommitHudCounterAnimState(0, 4, GEMCACHE_PHASE);
      nDelta = g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex] - GEMCACHE;
      if (nDelta >= 0xC9) {
        GEMCACHE = GEMCACHE + 8;
      } else if (nDelta >= 0x15 || GEMCACHE_PHASE == 0xC0) {
        GEMCACHE = GEMCACHE + 1;
      }
      if (g_nHudLevelGemCachedCount ==
              g_anLevelTotalGemsTable[g_nLevelIntroIndex] &&
          g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase == 0) {
        g_abHudCounterDisplayState[0] = 4;
      }
    }
  } else if (GEM_STATE == 3) {
    if (g_nHudLevelGemCachedCount !=
        g_anLevelGemsCollected[g_nLevelIntroIndex]) {
      GEM_STATE = 1;
    } else if (g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase == 0) {
      GEM_STATE = 0;
    } else {
      j = g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase - 1;
      g_bHudLevelGemRollPhase = j;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(0, 5, g_anHudRollOutStepTable[(unsigned char)j]);
    }
  } else if (GEM_STATE == 4) {
    GEM_TIMER = GEM_TIMER + g_nFrameStep;
    if (GEM_TIMER >= 0xF0) {
      GEM_STATE = 3;
      GEM_PHASE = 0xD;
    }
  }

  /* --- counter 1: dragons --------------------------------------------- */
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x2B1] += 8;
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x2AE] =
      (unsigned short)g_anCosineLut[g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x2B1]] >> 8;
  if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] == 1) {
    j = g_bHudDragonRollPhase & 0xFF;
    if (j == 0xD) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] = 2;
      g_bHudDragonRollPhase = 0;
      g_nHudDragonHoldTimer = -0x28;
    } else {
      g_bHudDragonRollPhase = j + 1;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(5, 3, g_anHudRollInStepTable[j]);
    }
  } else if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] == 2) {
    g_nHudDragonHoldTimer = g_nHudDragonHoldTimer + 1;
    if (g_nHudDragonHoldTimer == 0x14) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] = 3;
      g_bHudDragonRollPhase = 0xD;
    }
  } else if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] == 3) {
    if (g_bHudDragonRollPhase == 0) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[1] = 0;
    } else {
      j = g_bHudDragonRollPhase - 1;
      g_bHudDragonRollPhase = j;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(5, 3, g_anHudRollOutStepTable[(unsigned char)j]);
    }
  }

  /* --- counter 2: lives + sparx butterflies ---------------------------- */
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x3B6] = g_dwHudBobSinePhase;
  if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] == 0) {
    if (g_nHudLivesCachedCount != g_nExtraLives ||
        g_nHudButterflyCachedCount != g_nSparxFoodCount) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] = 1;
      g_bHudLivesRollPhase = 0;
    }
  } else if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] == 1) {
    j = g_bHudLivesRollPhase & 0xFF;
    if (j == 0xD) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] = 2;
      g_bHudLivesRollPhase = 0;
      g_nHudLivesHoldTimer = 0;
      if (g_nHudLivesCachedCount == g_nExtraLives &&
          g_nHudButterflyCachedCount == g_nSparxFoodCount) {
        g_nHudLivesHoldTimer = -0x28;
      }
    } else {
      g_bHudLivesRollPhase = j + 1;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(8, 3, g_anHudRollInStepTable[j]);
    }
  } else if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] == 2) {
    if (g_nHudLivesCachedCount == g_nExtraLives && g_bHudLivesRollPhase == 0) {
      if (g_nHudButterflyCachedCount == g_nSparxFoodCount) {
        g_nHudLivesHoldTimer = g_nHudLivesHoldTimer + 1;
        if (g_nHudLivesHoldTimer == 0x14) {
          g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] = 3;
          g_bHudLivesRollPhase = 0xD;
        }
      } else {
        g_nHudLivesHoldTimer = 0;
        g_nHudButterflyCachedCount = g_nSparxFoodCount;
      }
    } else {
      g_nHudLivesHoldTimer = 0;
      g_bHudLivesRollPhase -= 0x10;
      SetHudCounterDigits(8, 2, g_nHudLivesCachedCount + 1, 0);
      CommitHudCounterAnimState(8, 2, g_bHudLivesRollPhase);
      if (g_bHudLivesRollPhase == 0xC0) {
        g_nHudLivesCachedCount += 1;
      }
    }
  } else if (g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] == 3) {
    if (g_nHudLivesCachedCount != g_nExtraLives ||
        g_nHudButterflyCachedCount != g_nSparxFoodCount) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] = 1;
      g_nHudButterflyCachedCount = g_nSparxFoodCount;
    } else if (g_bHudLivesRollPhase == 0) {
      g_abHudCounterDisplayState[2] = 0;
    } else {
      j = g_bHudLivesRollPhase - 1;
      g_bHudLivesRollPhase = j;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(8, 3, g_anHudRollOutStepTable[(unsigned char)j]);
    }
  }

  /* lay the butterflies out around their ring anchor */
  if (g_anHudButterflyCachedBlock[0] > 0) {
    n = 0;
    j = 0;
    k = 0x60;
    do {
      n += 1;
      RECT(k) =
          (g_abHudButterflyRingXY[j] + g_anHudButterflyCachedBlock[0xE2]) -
          0x1D;
      RECT(k + 4) = 8;
      RECT(k + 6) = 8;
      RECT(k + 2) =
          (g_abHudButterflyRingXY[j + 1] + g_anHudButterflyCachedBlock[0xE3]) -
          0x1C;
      j += 2;
      k += 8;
    } while (n < g_anHudButterflyCachedBlock[0]);
  }

  /* --- counter 3: world eggs ------------------------------------------ */
  switch (EGG_STATE) {
  case 0:
    if (g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount != g_nWorldEggsRecovered ||
        g_nHudWorldEggRollRequest != 0) {
      EGG_STATE = 1;
      g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase = 0;
    }
    break;
  case 1:
    j = g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase & 0xFF;
    if (j == 0xD) {
      EGG_STATE = 2;
      g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer = 0;
      if (g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount == g_nWorldEggsRecovered &&
          g_nHudWorldEggRollRequest == 0) {
        g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer = -0x28;
      }
    } else {
      g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase = j + 1;
      OffsetHudDigitRollAxis(0, 0xC, -g_anHudRollInStepTable[j]);
    }
    break;
  case 2:
    if (g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount == g_nWorldEggsRecovered) {
      if (g_nHudWorldEggRollRequest != 0) {
        g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer = 0;
      } else if (g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer == 0x14) {
        EGG_STATE = 3;
        g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase = 0xD;
      }
    } else if (g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer == 1) {
      av[0] = g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount * 0x144 - 0x9C4;
      av[1] = 0x3F0;
      av[2] = 0x1000;
      (*(void (*)(int, int, int *, int))g_pfnLevelOverlayParticleSpawn)(
          0x10, 0x4D, av, 0);
    } else if (g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer >= 9) {
      g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount += 1;
      g_nHudWorldEggHoldTimer = 0;
    }
    g_anHudWorldEggTimerBlock[0] = g_anHudWorldEggTimerBlock[0] + 1;
    break;
  case 3:
    if (g_nHudWorldEggCachedCount != g_nWorldEggsRecovered ||
        g_nHudWorldEggRollRequest != 0) {
      EGG_STATE = 1;
    } else if (g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase == 0) {
      EGG_STATE = 0;
    } else {
      j = g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase - 1;
      g_bHudWorldEggRollPhase = j;
      OffsetHudDigitRollAxis(0, 0xC,
                             -g_anHudRollOutStepTable[(unsigned char)j]);
    }
    break;
  }

  /* --- counter 4: level eggs ------------------------------------------ */
  if (g_nLevelEggCount != 1) {
    g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount = g_nLevelEggCount;
  }
  switch (LEGG_STATE) {
  case 0:
    if (g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount != g_nLevelEggCount) {
      LEGG_STATE = 1;
      g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase = 0;
    }
    break;
  case 1:
    j = g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase & 0xFF;
    if (j == 0xD) {
      LEGG_STATE = 2;
      g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer = 0;
      if (g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount == g_nLevelEggCount) {
        g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer = -0x28;
      }
    } else {
      g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase = j + 1;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(0xB, 1, -g_anHudRollInStepTable[j]);
    }
    break;
  case 2:
    if (g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount != g_nLevelEggCount) {
      if (g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer == 0) {
        i = 0;
        nTint = 0x06000000;
        do {
          i += 1;
          (*(void (*)(int, int, unsigned char *,
                      int))g_pfnLevelOverlayParticleSpawn)(
              1, 0xC, &g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x3C8], nTint + 0x8080);
          nTint += 0x01000000;
        } while (i < 6);
      } else if (g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer >= 0xC) {
        g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x411] = 0x40;
        g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer = 0;
        g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount = g_nLevelEggCount;
      }
    } else if (g_nHudLevelEggHoldTimer == 0x14) {
      LEGG_STATE = 3;
      g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase = 0xD;
    }
    g_anHudLevelEggTimerBlock[0] = g_anHudLevelEggTimerBlock[0] + 1;
    break;
  case 3:
    if (g_nHudLevelEggCachedCount != g_nLevelEggCount) {
      LEGG_STATE = 1;
      g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase = 0;
    } else if (g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase == 0) {
      LEGG_STATE = 0;
    } else {
      j = g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase - 1;
      g_bHudLevelEggRollPhase = j;
      OffsetHudIconRollAxis(0xB, 1, -g_anHudRollOutStepTable[(unsigned char)j]);
    }
    break;
  }

  /* --- the level-egg icon spin, and butterflies -> extra lives --------- */
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x411] += 4;
  j = g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x411];
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x40C] = (unsigned short)g_anCosineLut[j] >> 7;
  g_abHudIconActorRecords[0x40D] = (unsigned short)g_anSineLut[j] >> 7;
  if (g_nSparxFoodCount >= 0x14) {
    g_nExtraLives = g_nExtraLives + 1;
    if (g_nExtraLives >= 0x64) {
      g_nExtraLives = 0x63;
    }
    g_nSparxFoodCount = g_nSparxFoodCount - 0x14;
  }
}
